68. ANN Accuracy: Recall

Suppose the exact search says the true nearest 10 documents are:

A B C D E F G H I J

Your ANN returns:

A B C D X Y G H P Q

It found:

A B C D G H

That's 6 of the actual 10.

Recall@10:

\[
Recall@10=\frac{6}{10}=60\%
\]

This gives us a way to evaluate ANN quality.


---

69. Recall vs Latency

This is one of the central engineering tradeoffs.

Imagine:

efSearch = 20

Latency: 5 ms
Recall: 90%

Increase search effort:

efSearch = 100

Latency: 15 ms
Recall: 98%

Increase again:

efSearch = 500

Latency: 50 ms
Recall: 99%

At some point the additional recall may not justify the additional latency.

Therefore production vector search is an optimization problem.


