70. The Curse of Dimensionality

Why can't we simply use ordinary spatial indexes forever?

Because high-dimensional spaces behave strangely.

In low dimensions:

2D
3D

geometric structures are relatively intuitive.

As dimensions increase:

100
384
768
1536

many traditional spatial intuitions break down.

Distances can become less discriminative.

This is one reason specialized ANN methods became important.


